# The toolchain pin is a dev/CI concern, and it must NOT reach the image builder.
# infra/docker/Dockerfile builds `FROM rust:1-slim-bookworm` (floating latest stable) and the
# official image ships rustup — so a rust-toolchain.toml in the build context would make the
# first `cargo` invocation rustup-fetch 1.93.1 plus rustfmt and clippy (which an image build
# has no use for) on EVERY build, and would break every production image build outright if
# that exact version ever became unavailable. Excluding it keeps image builds byte-for-byte
# as they were. The cleaner fix — pin the base image to rust:1.93.1-slim-bookworm so the
# toolchain file is a no-op there and dev/CI/image all agree — is a Dockerfile change and is
# deliberately out of Phase 4's scope.
rust-toolchain.toml
